  "RaStatText": "Resampling events gives 95\\% intervals of 22.7--35.6\\% for QAOA and 14.3--26.4\\% for annealing. On the 153 solvable events, the top QAOA sample was unsafe more often than the top annealing sample in 24 events and less often in 7 (Wilcoxon signed-rank $p=2.4\\times10^{-4}$), so the difference is consistent across events and not an effect of a few draws.",
