  "RaWorstCity": "Delhi",
  "RaWorstFalse": "27.1",
  "RaWorstGreedy": "72.9",
  "RaMinUnsafeCity": "87.7",
  "RaByCityText": "Unverified dispatch was unsafe in at least 87.7\\% of calls in every city. In Kolkata the three closures cut one of the six zones off from every shelter, so any instance with a group there has no valid plan, and only 4 of 60 were solvable. Delhi had the most false escalations (27.1\\%) and the weakest greedy rule, which found a plan in 72.9\\% of its solvable instances. The failures of the uncertified loop therefore depend on the city network as well as on the problem size.",
